{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLrof56dCg8qNgAsxTmS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: all four methods now raise `TypeError('Must pass only LinearEntity objects')` when either argument isn't a line-type object, instead of crashing with `AttributeError`.\n\nThe type check in `sympy/geometry/line.py` used `and`, so it only raised when *both* arguments were invalid. One bad argument got through and failed later when the code looked up `.direction`. I changed `and` to `or` in the check for `angle_between` (line 204), `smallest_angle_between` (239), `is_parallel` (616) and `is_perpendicular` (664).\n\nI ran the example from the issue against all four methods and each now raises the `TypeError`. The existing tests in `sympy/geometry/tests/test_line.py` all pass (36)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":18876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":571},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93180a5d-7eb5-4336-a921-f4bbcf336382","uuid":"d8ea9d85-89e4-4072-9837-e28a4cbabed8","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:08:48.549Z","request_id":"req_011ChLroeufkj4UfKw8h761x"}
